==Trivia==
*Blade is one character who was portrayed by an actor that exists in the Marvel Cinematic Universe without portraying themselves, alongside [[Mainframe]] and [[Gambit]]. [[Wesley Snipes]]' existence in the MCU was confirmed in the ''[[Luke Cage (TV series)|Luke Cage]]'' episode ''[[Now You're Mine]]''.

==Behind the Scenes==
*Blade in the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] continues the live-action incarnation from {{WPS|New Line Cinema}}'s {{WPS|Blade (Warner Bros. Pictures franchise)|''Blade'' trilogy}}, who was portrayed by both [[Wesley Snipes]] and {{WPS|Sticky Fingaz}}.
**[[Wesley Snipes]] mentioned during an interview with ''{{WPS|Deadline Hollywood}}'' back in July 2015 that he had been in discussions with [[Marvel Studios]] about reprising the role although those films don't share continuity with the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]].<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20150710071119/http://deadline.com/2015/07/wesley-snipes-blade-comic-con-interview-blade-the-player-1201472733/ Comic Con: Wesley Snipes On ‘Blade’ Marvel Talks, ‘The Player’ & Spike Lee]</ref> However, when [[Mahershala Ali]] was cast as the MCU's version of [[Blade]], Snipes himself approved Ali's casting.<ref>[https://comicbook.com/marvel/2019/07/23/blade-wesley-snipes-comments-on-mahershala-ali-casting/ Exclusive! Wesley Snipes Responds to Marvel Rebooting Blade]</ref>

